<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Discrete time ELBO</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section is organized as follows: First, we derive the expressions for the true posterior and the approximate posterior as outlined in Suppl. <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Generic case ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. We then simplify these expressions specifically for the case of absorbing state diffusion in Suppl. <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>. Finally, we derive the expression for the ELBO for absorbing state diffusion in Suppl. <a href="#A1.SS2.SSS3" title="A.2.3 Diffusion Loss ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Generic case</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the state transition matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, prior <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathit{\pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathit{\pi}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>, and the latent variables <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math>,
let</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{t|s}=\alpha_{t|s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{t|s}=\alpha_{t|s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.1 </span><math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the marginals in (<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ 2.2 Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ 2 Background ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) correspond to the following forward process:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{t};Q_{t|s}^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{t};Q_{t|s}^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{t};[\alpha_{t|s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}]^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{t};[\alpha_{t|s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}]^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{t};\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{s}+(1-\alpha_{t|s})\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}{\bm{1}}^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{t};\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{s}+(1-\alpha_{t|s})\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}{\bm{1}}^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because{\bm{1}}^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{s}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">∵</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn mathsize="0.800em">𝟏</mn><mo mathsize="0.800em">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because{\bm{1}}^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{s}=1</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{t};\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{s}+(1-\alpha_{t|s})\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝅</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{t};\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{s}+(1-\alpha_{t|s})\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The above equation indicates that during each diffusion step from <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\to t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\to t</annotation></semantics></math>,
a fraction <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha_{t|s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha_{t|s})</annotation></semantics></math> of the probability mass is transferred to the prior distribution <span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathit{\pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathit{\pi}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.2 </span><math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al. [1]</a></cite> show that the posterior corresponding to (<a href="#A1.Ex1" title="In A.1.1 𝑞(𝐳_𝑡|𝐳_𝑠) ‣ A.1 Generic case ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) is given as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}}{{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}}{{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which we simplify to the following:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}]{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}]^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}}{{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}[\alpha_{t}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{t}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}]^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}]{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}]^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}}{{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}[\alpha_{t}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{t}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}]^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]\odot[\alpha_{s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{s})\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}]}{{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}[\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t})\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}{\bm{1}}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}]}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝅</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]\odot[\alpha_{s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{s})\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}]}{{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}[\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t})\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}{\bm{1}}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}]}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]\odot[\alpha_{s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{s})\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}]}{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝅</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝅</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}^{\top}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]\odot[\alpha_{s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{s})\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}]}{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.E18.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A1.E18.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because{\bm{1}}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">∵</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn mathsize="0.800em">𝟏</mn><mo mathsize="0.800em">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because{\bm{1}}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}=1</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.3 </span><math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al. [1]</a></cite> approximate the reverse process in the following manner:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})=q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}=\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})=q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}=\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t):\mathcal{V}\times[0,1]\rightarrow\Delta^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t):\mathcal{V}\times[0,1]\rightarrow\Delta^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is an approximation for <math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Absorbing state</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the absorbing state diffusion process we have <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}{}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}{}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span><math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, takes only 2 values we consider the separate cases: <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the case <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> i.e. <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is unmasked.
From (<a href="#A1.Ex4" title="In A.1.2 𝑞(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡,𝐱) ‣ A.1 Generic case ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), we have the following:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}{\mathbf{m}}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}]\odot[\alpha_{s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}]}{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{x}}^{\top}{\mathbf{m}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}{\mathbf{m}}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}]\odot[\alpha_{s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}]}{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{x}}^{\top}{\mathbf{m}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{x}}]\odot[\alpha_{s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}]}{\alpha_{t}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{x}}]\odot[\alpha_{s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}]}{\alpha_{t}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex9.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because{\mathbf{x}}^{\top}{\mathbf{m}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">∵</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐦</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because{\mathbf{x}}^{\top}{\mathbf{m}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}}{\alpha_{t}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}}{\alpha_{t}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex10.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because{\mathbf{x}}\odot{\mathbf{m}}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">∵</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐦</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">𝟎</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because{\mathbf{x}}\odot{\mathbf{m}}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.Ex10.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and <math id="A1.Ex10.m2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=\alpha_{t|s}\alpha_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false" mathsize="1.780em">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=\alpha_{t|s}\alpha_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};{\mathbf{x}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};{\mathbf{x}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.E20.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A1.E20.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because\alpha_{t}=\alpha_{t|s}\alpha_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">∵</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">α</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because\alpha_{t}=\alpha_{t|s}\alpha_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, we have the following:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})=\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{s};{\mathbf{x}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})=\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{s};{\mathbf{x}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the case <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By substituting <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.Ex4" title="In A.1.2 𝑞(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡,𝐱) ‣ A.1 Generic case ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>),
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> simplifies to the following:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left(\frac{(\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}})\odot(\alpha_{s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}})}{(1-\alpha_{t})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left(\frac{(\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}})\odot(\alpha_{s}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}})}{(1-\alpha_{t})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left(\frac{(\alpha_{t|s}(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s})(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{x}})}{(1-\alpha_{t})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left(\frac{(\alpha_{t|s}(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s})(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{x}})}{(1-\alpha_{t})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{x}}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{x}}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that the above categorical distribution is non-zero for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{s}\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{s}\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and zero for every other value. The non-zero values are specified as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{1-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{1-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Combining Cases 1 and 2, we get:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})=\begin{cases}\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{s};{\mathbf{z}}_{t})&{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}},\\
\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{x}}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\right)&{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})=\begin{cases}\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}_{s};{\mathbf{z}}_{t})&amp;{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}},\\
\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{x}}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\right)&amp;{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span><math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the absorbing state diffusion process with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{$\bm{\mathit{\pi}}$}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we want to simplify the (<a href="#A1.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ A.1.3 𝑝_𝜃⁢(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡) ‣ A.1 Generic case ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>). For this reason, we consider 2 cases: first, when <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">case 1</span>), second, when <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">case 2</span>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the case when <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>. (<a href="#A1.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ A.1.3 𝑝_𝜃⁢(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡) ‣ A.1 Generic case ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) simplifies to the following:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{[Q_{t}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{[Q_{t}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}{\bm{1}}^{\top}]\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{[\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}{\bm{1}}^{\top}]\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{[\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}\langle{\bm{1}},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle]}{\alpha_{t}\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}\langle{\bm{1}},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle]}{\alpha_{t}\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex17.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">since <math id="A1.Ex17.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\bm{1}},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\bm{1}},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}]}{\alpha_{t}\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}]}{\alpha_{t}\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex19.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">since <math id="A1.Ex19.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot{\mathbf{m}}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot{\mathbf{m}}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{\alpha_{t}\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\odot\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{\alpha_{t}\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the case when <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>. (<a href="#A1.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ A.1.3 𝑝_𝜃⁢(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡) ‣ A.1 Generic case ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) simplifies to the following:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{{\mathbf{m}}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{{\mathbf{m}}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{[Q_{t}{\mathbf{m}}]^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{[Q_{t}{\mathbf{m}}]^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}{\bm{1}}^{\top}]\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{[\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t}){\bm{1}}]^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}{\bm{1}}^{\top}]\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}{[\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t}){\bm{1}}]^{\top}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}\langle{\bm{1}},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle]}{\alpha_{t}\langle{\mathbf{m}},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})\langle{\bm{1}},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}\langle{\bm{1}},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle]}{\alpha_{t}\langle{\mathbf{m}},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})\langle{\bm{1}},\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)\rangle}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}]}{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{m}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}]\odot[\alpha_{s}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}]}{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{m}}\odot\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t})\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}}{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{m}}\odot\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t})\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}}{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that the above categorical distribution, we can obtain the values for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math> which are as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})=\frac{(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t})\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})=\frac{(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t})\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})=\frac{\alpha_{s}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{s})}{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})=\frac{\alpha_{s}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{s})}{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">As a sanity check, we can verify that (<a href="#A1.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Case 2. ‣ A.2.2 𝑝_𝜃⁢(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) reduces to (<a href="#A1.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Case 2. ‣ A.2.1 𝑞(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡,𝐱) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), and (<a href="#A1.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Case 2. ‣ A.2.2 𝑝_𝜃⁢(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) reduces to (<a href="#A1.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Case 2. ‣ A.2.1 𝑞(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡,𝐱) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) if our denoising network can reconstruct <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> perfectly, i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Combining (<a href="#A1.Ex13" title="In Case 1. ‣ A.2.2 𝑝_𝜃⁢(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.Ex21" title="In Case 2. ‣ A.2.2 𝑝_𝜃⁢(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>), we get the following expression for the reverse process parameterization:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})=\begin{cases}\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\right)&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}$},\\
\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{m}}\odot\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t})\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}}{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}\right)&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}$.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">≠</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐦</mi></mrow><mtext mathsize="0.800em">.</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})=\begin{cases}\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\right)&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}$},\\
\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}_{s};\frac{\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{m}}\odot\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t})\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\alpha_{s}){\mathbf{m}}}{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}\right)&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}$.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.3 </span>Diffusion Loss</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a given <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{L}_{T}}=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\ldots,1\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}_{T}}=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\ldots,1\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math> denote the diffusion loss.
We break down the computation of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math> into 2 cases: <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">case 1</span>) and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">case 2</span>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1:</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">consider the case <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let’s simplify <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{D}_{\text{KL}}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{D}_{\text{KL}}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex27.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">From (<a href="#A1.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ Case 2. ‣ A.2.1 𝑞(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡,𝐱) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.Ex13" title="In Case 1. ‣ A.2.2 𝑝_𝜃⁢(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2:</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the case <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let’s simplify <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\mathbf{z}}_{s}}q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})}{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\mathbf{z}}_{s}}q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})}{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\mathbf{z}}_{s}\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}}q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})}{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\mathbf{z}}_{s}\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}}q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})}{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})}{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})}}_{\text{
Simplify using (\ref{eqn:d3pm_q_st_unmasked_old}) and (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_p_st_unmasked_old})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext> Simplify using (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Case 2. ‣ A.2.1 𝑞(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡,𝐱) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a></mtext><mtext>) and (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Case 2. ‣ A.2.2 𝑝_𝜃⁢(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})}{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})}}_{\text{
Simplify using (\ref{eqn:d3pm_q_st_unmasked_old}) and (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_p_st_unmasked_old})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt+\underbrace{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})}{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})}}_{\text{Simplify using (\ref{eqn:d3pm_q_st_masked_old}) and (\ref{eqn:d3pm_p_st_masked_old})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Simplify using (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Case 2. ‣ A.2.1 𝑞(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡,𝐱) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a></mtext><mtext>) and (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Case 2. ‣ A.2.2 𝑝_𝜃⁢(𝐳_𝑠|𝐳_𝑡) ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt+\underbrace{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})}{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})}}_{\text{Simplify using (\ref{eqn:d3pm_q_st_masked_old}) and (\ref{eqn:d3pm_p_st_masked_old})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}{(1-\alpha_{t})\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}{(1-\alpha_{t})\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt+\frac{1-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{(1-\alpha_{s})(\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t}))}{(1-\alpha_{t})(\alpha_{s}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{s}))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt+\frac{1-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{(1-\alpha_{s})(\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t}))}{(1-\alpha_{t})(\alpha_{s}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{s}))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math>
can be written in the following manner where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>
evaluates to 1 if <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> evaluates to 1 if <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}))}_{=0\;\text{, from (\ref{eqn:d3pm_kl_0_old})}}\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}\rangle+\underbrace{\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}))}_{\text{Given by (\ref{eqn:d3pm_kl_discrete_old})}}\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mtext>D</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>, from (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.Ex26" title="In Case 1: ‣ A.2.3 Diffusion Loss ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mtext>D</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Given by (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.Ex28" title="In Case 2: ‣ A.2.3 Diffusion Loss ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}))}_{=0\;\text{, from (\ref{eqn:d3pm_kl_0_old})}}\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}\rangle+\underbrace{\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}))}_{\text{Given by (\ref{eqn:d3pm_kl_discrete_old})}}\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we derive the diffusion loss, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}_{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}_{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, in the following manner:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}_{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}_{T}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\text{D}_{\text{KL}}(q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\bigg[\frac{\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}{(1-\alpha_{t})\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\bigg[\frac{\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}{(1-\alpha_{t})\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 102.43008pt+\frac{1-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{(1-\alpha_{s})(\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t}))}{(1-\alpha_{t})(\alpha_{s}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{s}))}\bigg]\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 102.43008pt+\frac{1-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{(1-\alpha_{s})(\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t}))}{(1-\alpha_{t})(\alpha_{s}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{s}))}\bigg]\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}_{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}_{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> is 0 if <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is an unmasked token i.e. <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.4 </span>NELBO</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al. [1]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sohl-Dickstein et al. [54]</a></cite> model <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i})_{i\in\{1,\dots,T\}}=1-\frac{i}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i})_{i\in\{1,\dots,T\}}=1-\frac{i}{T}</annotation></semantics></math> given latents <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{1,\dots,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{1,\dots,T}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, in this paper, we denote the latents as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0),\dots,t(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0),\dots,t(T)}</annotation></semantics></math>; and hence, the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> are given as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\alpha_{i})_{i\in\{1,\dots,T\}}=1-\frac{i}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\alpha_{i})_{i\in\{1,\dots,T\}}=1-\frac{i}{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex37.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">From <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al. [1]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sohl-Dickstein et al. [54]</a></cite>.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies(\alpha_{i})_{k\in\{1,\dots,T+1\}}=1-\frac{i}{T+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies(\alpha_{i})_{k\in\{1,\dots,T+1\}}=1-\frac{i}{T+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex38.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">For <math id="A1.Ex38.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T+1</annotation></semantics></math> latents</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies(\alpha_{i})_{i\in\{0,\dots,T\}}=1-\frac{i+1}{T+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies(\alpha_{i})_{i\in\{0,\dots,T\}}=1-\frac{i+1}{T+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex39.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Offsetting the indices by 1.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies(\alpha_{{t(i)}})_{i\in\{0,\dots,T\}}=1-\frac{i+1}{T+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies(\alpha_{{t(i)}})_{i\in\{0,\dots,T\}}=1-\frac{i+1}{T+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.E35.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Switching the notations from <math id="A1.E35.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.E35.m2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Consequently, from Equation <a href="#A1.Ex37" title="In A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>, we derive that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{t(0)}=\frac{T}{T+1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{t(0)}=\frac{T}{T+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{t(T)}=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{t(T)}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus we have the following:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}\sim\text{Cat}(.;\alpha_{t=0}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t=0}){\mathbf{m}})=\text{Cat}\left(.;\frac{T}{T+1}{\mathbf{x}}+\frac{1}{T+1}{\mathbf{m}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}\sim\text{Cat}(.;\alpha_{t=0}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t=0}){\mathbf{m}})=\text{Cat}\left(.;\frac{T}{T+1}{\mathbf{x}}+\frac{1}{T+1}{\mathbf{m}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}})=\text{Cat}(.;\alpha_{t=1}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t=1}){\mathbf{m}})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}})=\text{Cat}(.;\alpha_{t=1}{\mathbf{x}}+(1-\alpha_{t=1}){\mathbf{m}})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The NELBO (<a href="#S2.EGx1" title="2.1 Diffusion Models ‣ 2 Background ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>) simplifies to the following:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+\underbrace{{\mathcal{L}_{T}}}_{\text{Compute using \penalty\ (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_diffusion_loss})}}\right]+\underbrace{D_{\mathrm{KL}}[q({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}})\|p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)})]}_{=0\;\;\text{using \penalty\ (\ref{supp:eqn:d3pm_qT}) and (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_prior})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Compute using  (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.Ex35" title="In Case 2: ‣ A.2.3 Diffusion Loss ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.560em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>using  (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E39" title="Equation 39 ‣ A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a></mtext><mtext>) and (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+\underbrace{{\mathcal{L}_{T}}}_{\text{Compute using \penalty\ (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_diffusion_loss})}}\right]+\underbrace{D_{\mathrm{KL}}[q({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}})\|p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)})]}_{=0\;\;\text{using \penalty\ (\ref{supp:eqn:d3pm_qT}) and (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_prior})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q,t}\Bigg[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+T\bigg[\frac{\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}{(1-\alpha_{t})\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q,t}\Bigg[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+T\bigg[\frac{\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t})}{(1-\alpha_{t})\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 110.96556pt+\frac{1-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{(1-\alpha_{s})(\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t}))}{(1-\alpha_{t})(\alpha_{s}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{s}))}\bigg]\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 110.96556pt+\frac{1-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{(1-\alpha_{s})(\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{t}))}{(1-\alpha_{t})(\alpha_{s}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle+(1-\alpha_{s}))}\bigg]\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>MDLM</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we show how SUBS parameterization can simplify the functional form of the NELBO as defined in (<a href="#A1.Ex40" title="In A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Rao-Blackwellization</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We employ the RB techniques as described in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS3" title="3.2.3 SUBS Parameterization ‣ 3.2 Masked Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.3</span></a> to simplify the
NELBO (<a href="#A1.Ex40" title="In A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) to (<a href="#A2.Ex43" title="In B.1.1 Zero Masking Probabilities ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) using RB2, and further
to (<a href="#A2.Ex44" title="In B.1.3 NELBO ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) using RB1.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.1 </span>Zero Masking Probabilities</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using “Zero Masking Probabilities” (RB2) from Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS3" title="3.2.3 SUBS Parameterization ‣ 3.2 Masked Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.3</span></a>, we set <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.Ex35" title="In Case 2: ‣ A.2.3 Diffusion Loss ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) to obtain the following simplified diffusion loss:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2}}_{T}}=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\left[\frac{\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{1}{\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}\right]\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mtext>RB2</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2}}_{T}}=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\left[\frac{\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{1}{\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}\right]\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log{\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}\right]\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log{\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}\right]\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The corresponding Rao-Blackwellized NELBO is given as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+\underbrace{{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2}}_{T}}}_{\text{Compute using \penalty\ (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_diffusion_loss_rb2})}}\right]+\underbrace{D_{\mathrm{KL}}[q({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}})\|p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)})]}_{=0\;\;\text{using \penalty\ (\ref{supp:eqn:d3pm_qT}) and (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_prior})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mtext>RB2</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Compute using  (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A2.Ex42" title="In B.1.1 Zero Masking Probabilities ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.560em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>using  (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E39" title="Equation 39 ‣ A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a></mtext><mtext>) and (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+\underbrace{{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2}}_{T}}}_{\text{Compute using \penalty\ (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_diffusion_loss_rb2})}}\right]+\underbrace{D_{\mathrm{KL}}[q({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}})\|p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)})]}_{=0\;\;\text{using \penalty\ (\ref{supp:eqn:d3pm_qT}) and (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_prior})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q,t}\left[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log{\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}\right]\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q,t}\left[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log{\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}\right]\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.2 </span>Carry Over Unmasking</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that the term <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.Ex42" title="In B.1.1 Zero Masking Probabilities ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) is intended to reduce the diffusion loss to zero when <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, we will demonstrate that, by applying “Carry Over Unmasking” (RB1) from Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS3" title="3.2.3 SUBS Parameterization ‣ 3.2 Masked Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.3</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> can be removed from (<a href="#A2.Ex42" title="In B.1.1 Zero Masking Probabilities ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that RB1 guarantees <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, with the RB1 parameterization, the diffusion loss in (<a href="#A2.Ex42" title="In B.1.1 Zero Masking Probabilities ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) becomes zero for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{m}}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> can be safely omitted from (<a href="#A2.Ex43" title="In B.1.1 Zero Masking Probabilities ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), yielding the following diffusion loss:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2 + RB1}}_{T}}=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log{\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mtext>RB2 + RB1</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2 + RB1}}_{T}}=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log{\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.3 </span>NELBO</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we have the following NELBO:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+\underbrace{{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2 + RB1}}_{T}}}_{\text{Compute using \penalty\ (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_elbo_rb2_rb1})}}\right]+\underbrace{D_{\mathrm{KL}}[q({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}})\|p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)})]}_{\text{$=0$ using \penalty\ (\ref{supp:eqn:d3pm_qT}) and (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_prior})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mtext>RB2 + RB1</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Compute using  (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A2.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ B.1.2 Carry Over Unmasking ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mtext> using  (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E39" title="Equation 39 ‣ A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a></mtext><mtext>) and (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+\underbrace{{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2 + RB1}}_{T}}}_{\text{Compute using \penalty\ (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_elbo_rb2_rb1})}}\right]+\underbrace{D_{\mathrm{KL}}[q({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}})\|p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)})]}_{\text{$=0$ using \penalty\ (\ref{supp:eqn:d3pm_qT}) and (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_prior})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q,t}\left[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log{\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q,t}\left[-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})+T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log{\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle}\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS3.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Comparing (<a href="#A2.Ex44" title="In B.1.3 NELBO ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.Ex43" title="In B.1.1 Zero Masking Probabilities ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that due to RB1, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.Ex44" title="In B.1.3 NELBO ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) reduces to 0 every time <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> as explained in (<a href="#A2.Ex47" title="In B.2.2 Reconstruction Loss ‣ B.2 Continuous Time ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>). However, this is not the case in (<a href="#A2.Ex43" title="In B.1.1 Zero Masking Probabilities ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), even though it has a functionally similar expression to (<a href="#A2.Ex44" title="In B.1.3 NELBO ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>). Because of this reason (<a href="#A2.Ex44" title="In B.1.3 NELBO ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) should lead to a better likelihood estimate and we empirically verify this in Table <a href="#S5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 5.3 Ablation Analysis ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Continuous Time</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.1 </span>Diffusion Loss</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To derive the continuous-time diffusion loss, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{diffusion}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{diffusion}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the limiting case <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{T\to\infty}{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2 + RB1}}_{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mtext>RB2 + RB1</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{T\to\infty}{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2 + RB1}}_{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A2.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ B.1.2 Carry Over Unmasking ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{diffusion}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{diffusion}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2 + RB1}}_{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi><mtext>RB2 + RB1</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}{\mathcal{L}^{\text{RB2 + RB1}}_{T}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\},q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\lim_{T\to\infty}T\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\dots,1\right\},q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\lim_{T\to\infty}T\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1],q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1],q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.E46.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using <math id="A2.E46.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{T\to\infty}T(\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s})=\alpha^{\prime}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{T\to\infty}T(\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s})=\alpha^{\prime}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.2 </span>Reconstruction Loss</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the continous time case, from (<a href="#A1.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}\sim\lim_{T\to\infty}\text{Cat}\left(.;\frac{T}{T+1}{\mathbf{x}}+\frac{1}{T+1}{\mathbf{m}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">∼</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}\sim\lim_{T\to\infty}\text{Cat}\left(.;\frac{T}{T+1}{\mathbf{x}}+\frac{1}{T+1}{\mathbf{m}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\implies{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}\sim\text{Cat}\left(.;{\mathbf{x}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}\sim\text{Cat}\left(.;{\mathbf{x}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the reconstruction loss reduces to 0 in the following manner:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}_{\text{recons}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>recons</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}_{\text{recons}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}={\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)}={\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex50.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">From (<a href="#A2.Ex47" title="In B.2.2 Reconstruction Loss ‣ B.2 Continuous Time ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}},t(0)),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}},t(0)),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log\langle{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log\langle{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex52.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Due to “carry-over unmasking” <math id="A2.Ex52.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}},t(0))={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}},t(0))={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.3 </span>NELBO</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we have the following NELBO:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[-\underbrace{\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})}_{\text{ $=0$ from\penalty\ (\ref{supp:eqn:mdlm_loss_recons})}}+\underbrace{{\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{diffusion}}}}_{\text{Compute using \penalty\ (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_elbo_rb2_rb1})}}\right]+\underbrace{D_{\mathrm{KL}}[q({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}})\|p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)},t)]}_{\text{$=0$ using \penalty\ (\ref{supp:eqn:d3pm_qT}) and (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_prior})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext> </mtext><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mtext> from (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A2.Ex49" title="In B.2.2 Reconstruction Loss ‣ B.2 Continuous Time ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Compute using  (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A2.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ B.1.2 Carry Over Unmasking ‣ B.1 Rao-Blackwellization ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mtext> using  (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E39" title="Equation 39 ‣ A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a></mtext><mtext>) and (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A1.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ A.2.4 NELBO ‣ A.2 Absorbing state ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[-\underbrace{\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(0)})}_{\text{ $=0$ from\penalty\ (\ref{supp:eqn:mdlm_loss_recons})}}+\underbrace{{\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{diffusion}}}}_{\text{Compute using \penalty\ (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_elbo_rb2_rb1})}}\right]+\underbrace{D_{\mathrm{KL}}[q({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}})\|p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t(T)},t)]}_{\text{$=0$ using \penalty\ (\ref{supp:eqn:d3pm_qT}) and (\ref{subsec:eqn:d3pm_prior})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boxed{\mathbb{E}_{q,t}\left[\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boxed{\mathbb{E}_{q,t}\left[\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Final Algorithm</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ B.3 Final Algorithm ‣ Appendix B MDLM ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we present the training algorithm for MDLM.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Training MDLM</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">repeat</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
                <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}\sim q(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}\sim q(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Sample a sentence.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
                <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Sample a time step.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
                <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\sim\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t};\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}+(1-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\sim\text{Cat}({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t};\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}+(1-\alpha_{t}){\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∀</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq\ell\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq\ell\leq L</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Mask Each token <math id="alg1.l4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> independently to obtain the latent <math id="alg1.l4.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}^{1:L}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}^{1:L}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
                Take gradient descent step on

<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{\ell}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}^{\ell}({\mathbf{z}}^{1:L}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}\rangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{\ell}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}^{\ell}({\mathbf{z}}^{1:L}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">until</span> converged

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Concrete Score Matching</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the previous section, we defined the discrete diffusion process as a Discrete-Time Markov Chain (DTMC) with a finite set of <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> states, <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{\{0,\frac{1}{T},\dots,1\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{\{0,\frac{1}{T},\dots,1\}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a state transition matrix <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. To derive the continuous-time ELBO, we simply take the limit as <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Campbell et al. [5]</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. [33]</a></cite> defined the discrete diffusion process as a Continuous-Time Markov Chain (CTMC), where the forward corruption process is specified by the rate change matrix <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{V}|\times|\mathcal{V}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{V}|\times|\mathcal{V}|}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be thought of as the instantaneous rate at which one state transitions to another. With this formulation, the forward posterior <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> and the true reverse posterior <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed in terms of the rate change matrix as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{y}})=\delta_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}}}+R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{y}})=\delta_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}}}+R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})=\delta_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}}}+\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})=\delta_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}}}+\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the Kroenecker delta and <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{T^{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{T^{2}})</annotation></semantics></math> represents higher order terms of <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{T^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{T^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In Sec. <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, we show how to express the rate matrix <math id="A3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the state transition matrix <math id="A3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. [33]</a></cite> propose a continuous time ELBO for this process.
They mention that this expression can be derived from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Benton et al. [4]</a></cite>, though they do not provide an explicit derivation. For this reason, we present a rigorous derivation in Sec. <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 NELBO ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> and further demonstrate that, under the SUBS parameterization in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS3" title="3.2.3 SUBS Parameterization ‣ 3.2 Masked Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.3</span></a>, this formula reduces to our proposed continuous-time ELBO, given by (<a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 3.4 Continuous-Time Likelihood Bounds ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the remainder of this section, we switch to the notation <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> to denote <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}_{s}={\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, aligning with the notation typically used in the CTMC literature.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Extracting the Rate Matrix</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we aim to express the rate change matrix <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the state transition matrix <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. To do this, we first represent the forward transition <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{t|s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{t|s}}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> separately, allowing us to illustrate their relationship.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using (<a href="#A1.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ A.1 Generic case ‣ Appendix A Discrete time ELBO ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), we can write <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{t|s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{t|s}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}[\alpha_{t|s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}{\mathbf{m}}^{\top}]^{\top}{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}[\alpha_{t|s}\mathbf{I}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\bm{1}}{\mathbf{m}}^{\top}]^{\top}{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{y}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\mathbf{m}}{\bm{1}}^{\top}{\mathbf{y}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{y}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\mathbf{m}}{\bm{1}}^{\top}{\mathbf{y}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{y}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\mathbf{m}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}[\alpha_{t|s}{\mathbf{y}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s}){\mathbf{m}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{t|s}[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}{\mathbf{y}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s})[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{t|s}[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}{\mathbf{y}}+(1-\alpha_{t|s})[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Now let’s analyze all possible combinations for the tuple <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">1. Case <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using (<a href="#A3.Ex55" title="In C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>),
we find that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})=\alpha_{t|s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})=\alpha_{t|s}</annotation></semantics></math> for the DTMC. By (<a href="#A3.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>), we have <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})=1+R_{t}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})\frac{1}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})=1+R_{t}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})\frac{1}{T}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, since the higher-order terms <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> vanish in the limit. Thus, we get:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{T\to\infty}\left[1+R_{t}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})\frac{1}{T}\right]=\lim_{T\to\infty}\alpha_{t|s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{T\to\infty}\left[1+R_{t}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})\frac{1}{T}\right]=\lim_{T\to\infty}\alpha_{t|s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies R_{t}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})=\lim_{T\to\infty}T(\alpha_{t|s}-1)=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies R_{t}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}})=\lim_{T\to\infty}T(\alpha_{t|s}-1)=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">2. Case <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\in\mathcal{V}-\{{\mathbf{m}}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\in\mathcal{V}-\{{\mathbf{m}}\})</annotation></semantics></math>:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, using (<a href="#A3.Ex55" title="In C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>), we have <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=1-\alpha_{t|s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=1-\alpha_{t|s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})\frac{1}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})\frac{1}{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{T\to\infty}\left[R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})\frac{1}{T}\right]=\lim_{T\to\infty}[1-\alpha_{t|s}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{T\to\infty}\left[R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})\frac{1}{T}\right]=\lim_{T\to\infty}[1-\alpha_{t|s}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=\lim_{T\to\infty}T(1-\alpha_{t|s})=-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=\lim_{T\to\infty}T(1-\alpha_{t|s})=-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">3. Case <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using (<a href="#A3.Ex55" title="In C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) and(<a href="#A3.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>), we find <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{m}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{m}})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{m}})=1+R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{m}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{t|s}}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{m}})=1+R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{m}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since these two expressions must be equal for any <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{m}})=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{m}})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that when <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math> is constant, the term <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to zero, as it includes higher-order time derivatives of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">4. Case <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{y}}\in\mathcal{V}-\{{\mathbf{x}}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{y}}\in\mathcal{V}-\{{\mathbf{x}}\})</annotation></semantics></math>:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the context of absorbing state diffusion, these states are never observed. Thus,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{y}}\in\mathcal{V}-\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{y}}\in\mathcal{V}-\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">5. Case <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}-\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\},{\mathbf{y}}\in\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}-\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\},{\mathbf{y}}\in\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\})</annotation></semantics></math>:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the context of absorbing state diffusion, these states are never observed. Thus,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}-\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\},{\mathbf{y}}\in\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}-\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\},{\mathbf{y}}\in\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we can express the forward rate matrix as:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{R_{t}=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left(\mathbf{I}-{\mathbf{m}}{\bm{1}}^{\top}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{R_{t}=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left(\mathbf{I}-{\mathbf{m}}{\bm{1}}^{\top}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">It can be seen that the columns of this matrix sum to zero, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})=0\implies R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})=\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})=0\implies R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})=\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which ensures that the probability mass is preserved in the forward diffusion process. Similarly, the reverse rate matrix <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written in terms of the forward rate matrix <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})=\begin{cases}\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}$}\\
-\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}\frac{q_{t}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},\tilde{\mathbf{y}})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{y}}$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">≠</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})=\begin{cases}\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}$}\\
-\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}\frac{q_{t}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},\tilde{\mathbf{y}})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{y}}$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>NELBO</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Meng et al. [37]</a></cite> introduced the term “concrete score” for the term <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})/q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})/q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> that appears in <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since this quantity is not directly accessible in the reverse diffusion process, we approximate it using a neural network, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}:\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}:\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, with parameters <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. The approximate reverse posterior <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{s|t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{s|t}}</annotation></semantics></math> can then be expressed in terms of the approximate reverse rate matrix <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in the following manner:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{p_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}})=\delta_{y^{\prime},y}+\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{p_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}})=\delta_{y^{\prime},y}+\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})=\begin{cases}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}$}\\
-\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},\tilde{\mathbf{y}})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{y}}$}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">≠</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})=\begin{cases}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}$}\\
-\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},\tilde{\mathbf{y}})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{y}}$}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the approximate concrete score <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})/q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})/q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. [33]</a></cite> propose the following NELBO to train such a model:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(a)=a\log a-a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(a)=a\log a-a</annotation></semantics></math>. They mention that this expression can be derived from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Benton et al. [4]</a></cite>, though they do not provide an explicit derivation. For this reason, we present a rigorous derivation in the following section.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let’s focus on the diffusion loss for this process. As mentioned in the previous section, the reconstruction and prior loss terms reduce to zero. The continuous-time diffusion loss is given by:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{T\to\infty}T\mathbb{E}_{t\in\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\ldots,1\},{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}[\text{D}_{\text{KL}}({q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\|p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{T\to\infty}T\mathbb{E}_{t\in\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\ldots,1\},{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}[\text{D}_{\text{KL}}({q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\|p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\mathbb{E}_{t\in\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\ldots,1\},{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\mathbb{E}_{t\in\{\frac{1}{T},\frac{2}{T},\ldots,1\},{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\lim_{T\to\infty}T\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mi>T</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\lim_{T\to\infty}T\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\underbrace{\lim_{T\to\infty}T{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}}_{\textbf{Term 1}}+\underbrace{\lim_{T\to\infty}T\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}}_{\textbf{Term 2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Term 1</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Term 2</mtext></munder><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\underbrace{\lim_{T\to\infty}T{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}}_{\textbf{Term 1}}+\underbrace{\lim_{T\to\infty}T\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}}_{\textbf{Term 2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let’s simplify these two terms separately. For the derivation, we’ll rely on two key observations: In the limiting case as <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows from (<a href="#A3.E51" title="Equation 51 ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) that <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{T\to\infty}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{T\to\infty}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and from (<a href="#A3.E61" title="Equation 61 ‣ C.2 NELBO ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>) that <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{T\to\infty}{p_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{T\to\infty}{p_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Term 1:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{T\to\infty}T{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{T\to\infty}T{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex64.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because\lim_{T\to\infty}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.1389em">∵</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because\lim_{T\to\infty}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.Ex64.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; hence,</span></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex66.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">The above term is in <math id="A3.Ex66.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty\times 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty\times 0</annotation></semantics></math> indeterminate form; therefore,</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\left(\log{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})-\log{p_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\left(\log{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})-\log{p_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex68.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Substituting <math id="A3.Ex68.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{s|t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false" mathsize="1.780em">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{s|t}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Ex68.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{s|t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false" mathsize="1.780em">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{s|t}}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A3.E51" title="Equation 51 ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E61" title="Equation 61 ‣ C.2 NELBO ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>), we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\left[\log\left(1+\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)\right)-\log\left(1+\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\left[\log\left(1+\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)\right)-\log\left(1+\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex70.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Applying the Taylor series expansion for <math id="A3.Ex70.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\left[\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)-\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}-\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\left[\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)-\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})\frac{1}{T}-\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})+\lim_{T\to\infty}T\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)-\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})-\lim_{T\to\infty}T\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})+\lim_{T\to\infty}T\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)-\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})-\lim_{T\to\infty}T\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex73.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A3.Ex73.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because\lim_{T\to\infty}T\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.1389em">∵</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because\lim_{T\to\infty}T\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.Ex73.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, we get:</span></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})-\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})-\tilde{R}^{\theta}_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex75.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#A3.E60" title="Equation 60 ‣ 5. Case (𝐲^′∈𝒱-{𝐦,𝐱},𝐲∈{𝐦,𝐱}): ‣ C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E62" title="Equation 62 ‣ C.2 NELBO ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>), we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Term 2:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{T\to\infty}T\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{T\to\infty}T\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})\log\frac{{q_{s|t}}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}{p_{s|t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex77.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Substituting <math id="A3.Ex77.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q_{s|t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false" mathsize="1.780em">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q_{s|t}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Ex77.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{s|t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false" mathsize="1.780em">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{s|t}}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A3.E51" title="Equation 51 ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E61" title="Equation 61 ‣ C.2 NELBO ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>), we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}\left[\left[\frac{q_{s}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)\right]\log\frac{\frac{q_{s}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)}{{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\to\infty}T\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}\left[\left[\frac{q_{s}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)\right]\log\frac{\frac{q_{s}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)}{{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\frac{1}{T}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\right)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
