</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, plugging (<a href="#A3.Ex63" title="In Term 1: ‣ C.2 NELBO ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.Ex76" title="In Term 2: ‣ C.2 NELBO ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>) into (<a href="#A3.Ex60" title="In Proof. ‣ C.2 NELBO ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>) yields us the NELBO as proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. [33]</a></cite>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\Bigg[-\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\Bigg[-\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 73.12378pt+\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\Bigg(\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}\Bigg)\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 73.12378pt+\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\Bigg(\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}\Bigg)\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\Bigg[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\Bigg(-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}+{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\Bigg[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\Bigg(-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}+{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 145.10922pt+\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}\Bigg)\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 145.10922pt+\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}\Bigg)\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boxed{\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boxed{\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(a)=a\log a-a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(a)=a\log a-a</annotation></semantics></math>. This concludes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Concrete Score for MDLM</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a latent variable <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the output of the denoising model, <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> parameterized using SUBS, we aim to recover the concrete score <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})\in(\mathbb{R}^{+}+\{0\})^{|\mathcal{V}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})\in(\mathbb{R}^{+}+\{0\})^{|\mathcal{V}|}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})_{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐲</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})_{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>
is the ratio <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{p_{t}({\mathbf{y}})}{p_{t}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{p_{t}({\mathbf{y}})}{p_{t}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math> in the reverse process. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> approximates <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}({\mathbf{y}})=q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}({\mathbf{y}})=q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))</annotation></semantics></math>; therefore,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})_{\mathbf{y}}=\frac{p_{t}({\mathbf{y}})}{p_{t}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})}=\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))}{q_{t}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐲</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})_{\mathbf{y}}=\frac{p_{t}({\mathbf{y}})}{p_{t}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})}=\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))}{q_{t}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To obtain the score, we first compute <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))</annotation></semantics></math> for all possible <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.1 Interpolating Discrete Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), we derive the following expressions under the SUBS parameterization:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}},t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{y}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{y}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}\not\in\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}},t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}\not\in\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}},t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{z}}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}},t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{z}}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}},t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\in\mathcal{V},t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}|\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\in\mathcal{V},t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Plugging these into (<a href="#A3.E68" title="Equation 68 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>), we get:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{y}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{y}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.E73.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#A3.E72" title="Equation 72 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E69" title="Equation 69 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.E74.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#A3.E72" title="Equation 72 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}}=\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}}=\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.E75.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#A3.E71" title="Equation 71 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E72" title="Equation 72 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{z}}_{t}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{z}}_{t}}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.E76.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#A3.E71" title="Equation 71 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}\not\in\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}\not\in\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.E77.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#A3.E70" title="Equation 70 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E71" title="Equation 71 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">These can be consolidated into the following expression:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})_{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{y}}^{\top}\left[\delta_{{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}}\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\delta_{{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}})\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}{\mathbf{m}}+{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐲</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t})_{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{y}}^{\top}\left[\delta_{{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}}\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)+(1-\delta_{{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{m}}})\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}{\mathbf{m}}+{\mathbf{z}}_{t}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Reverse Rate Matrix for MDLM</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We can formulate the reverse rate matrix for MDLM using (<a href="#A3.E78" title="Equation 78 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">78</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E58" title="Equation 58 ‣ 5. Case (𝐲^′∈𝒱-{𝐦,𝐱},𝐲∈{𝐦,𝐱}): ‣ C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>). Recall that the reverse rate matrix <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex86.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}$}\\
-\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},\tilde{\mathbf{y}})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{y}}$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">≠</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}$}\\
-\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}},\tilde{\mathbf{y}})&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{y}}$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let’s examine the cases where <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the reverse rate <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex87.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex89.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#A3.E73" title="Equation 73 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E58" title="Equation 58 ‣ 5. Case (𝐲^′∈𝒱-{𝐦,𝐱},𝐲∈{𝐦,𝐱}): ‣ C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>), we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\rangle\left[-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\rangle\left[-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the reverse rate <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex91.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\tilde{R}_{t}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\tilde{R}_{t}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex93.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#A3.Ex87" title="In Case 𝐲=𝐦: ‣ C.4 Reverse Rate Matrix for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">79</span></a>), we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex96.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">“zero-masking probability” in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS3" title="3.2.3 SUBS Parameterization ‣ 3.2 Masked Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.3</span></a> <math id="A3.Ex96.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\implies\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\rangle=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="1.780em">~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="1.250em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\implies\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\rangle=1</annotation></semantics></math>; hence,</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> we have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex97.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\notin\{{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\notin\{{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\notin\{{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\}}\underbrace{R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\notin\{{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\})}_{\text{$=0$ from\penalty\ (\ref{eqn:mdlm_rate_matrix})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mtext> from (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A3.E58" title="Equation 58 ‣ 5. Case (𝐲^′∈𝒱-{𝐦,𝐱},𝐲∈{𝐦,𝐱}): ‣ C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\notin\{{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\}}\underbrace{R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\notin\{{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\})}_{\text{$=0$ from\penalty\ (\ref{eqn:mdlm_rate_matrix})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex99.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}}}\underbrace{R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}})}_{\text{$=0$ from\penalty\ (\ref{eqn:mdlm_rate_matrix})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mtext> from (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A3.E58" title="Equation 58 ‣ 5. Case (𝐲^′∈𝒱-{𝐦,𝐱},𝐲∈{𝐦,𝐱}): ‣ C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}}}\underbrace{R_{t}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}})}_{\text{$=0$ from\penalty\ (\ref{eqn:mdlm_rate_matrix})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, for <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex101.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}\tilde{R}_{t}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}}\tilde{R}_{t}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\underbrace{\tilde{R}_{t}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})}_{\text{$=0$ from\penalty\ (\ref{eqn:mdlm_reverse_rate_3})}}-\underbrace{\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\notin\{{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\}}\tilde{R}_{t}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})}_{\text{$=0$ from\penalty\ (\ref{eqn:mdlm_reverse_rate_2})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mtext> from (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A3.Ex99" title="In Case 𝐲≠𝐦: ‣ C.4 Reverse Rate Matrix for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">82</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mtext> from (</mtext><mtext><a href="#A3.Ex97" title="In Case 𝐲≠𝐦: ‣ C.4 Reverse Rate Matrix for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\underbrace{\tilde{R}_{t}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})}_{\text{$=0$ from\penalty\ (\ref{eqn:mdlm_reverse_rate_3})}}-\underbrace{\sum_{\tilde{\mathbf{y}}\notin\{{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\}}\tilde{R}_{t}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}})}_{\text{$=0$ from\penalty\ (\ref{eqn:mdlm_reverse_rate_2})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Summarizing (<a href="#A3.Ex87" title="In Case 𝐲=𝐦: ‣ C.4 Reverse Rate Matrix for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">79</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.Ex91" title="In Case 𝐲=𝐦: ‣ C.4 Reverse Rate Matrix for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">80</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.Ex97" title="In Case 𝐲≠𝐦: ‣ C.4 Reverse Rate Matrix for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.Ex99" title="In Case 𝐲≠𝐦: ‣ C.4 Reverse Rate Matrix for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">82</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.Ex101" title="In Case 𝐲≠𝐦: ‣ C.4 Reverse Rate Matrix for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">83</span></a>), we have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{R}_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime},{\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex104.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}-\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}},t),{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\rangle\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}$}\\
\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}$}\\
0&amp;\text{\footnotesize otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">≠</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐦</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐦</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐦</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext mathsize="0.800em">otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}-\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}},t),{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\rangle\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}$}\\
\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}&amp;\text{\footnotesize${\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{m}}$}\\
0&amp;\text{\footnotesize otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boxed{-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}[\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}},t)-{\mathbf{m}}]\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boxed{-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}[{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}]^{\top}[\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{y}},t)-{\mathbf{m}}]\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Deriving MDLM’s NELBO via CTMC</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we aim to show that substituting the expression for the rate matrix <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of state transition matrix <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A3.E58" title="Equation 58 ‣ 5. Case (𝐲^′∈𝒱-{𝐦,𝐱},𝐲∈{𝐦,𝐱}): ‣ C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>) into (<a href="#A3.Ex82" title="In Term 2: ‣ C.2 NELBO ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>) and switching from score-parameterization to the SUBS parameterization (Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS3" title="3.2.3 SUBS Parameterization ‣ 3.2 Masked Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.3</span></a>) yields the simplified NELBO for MDLM as given by (<a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 3.4 Continuous-Time Likelihood Bounds ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>). We present the proof below. Recall that the term <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{a},\mathbf{b}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{a},\mathbf{b}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the dot product of two vectors <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}</annotation></semantics></math> represent two <span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">one-hot</span> vectors, this quantity evaluates to <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}=\mathbf{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐛</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}=\mathbf{b}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that for absorbing state diffusion, <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> takes only two possible values, i.e., <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we expand (<a href="#A3.Ex82" title="In Term 2: ‣ C.2 NELBO ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>) as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex105.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\Bigg[\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{x}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\Bigg[\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{x}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 68.28644pt+\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 68.28644pt+\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex107.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A3.Ex107.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because R_{t}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{x}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">∵</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">≠</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because R_{t}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{x}})=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.Ex107.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> from (<a href="#A3.E56" title="Equation 56 ‣ 4. Case (𝐲^′=𝐱,𝐲∈𝒱-{𝐱}): ‣ C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>), we get:</span></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex109.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Substituting <math id="A3.Ex109.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}({\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A3.Ex59" title="In 2. Case (𝐲^′=𝐦,𝐲∈𝒱-{𝐦}): ‣ C.1 Extracting the Rate Matrix ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>), we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left({\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}+K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E85.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left(\underbrace{\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}}_{\textbf{Term 1}}-\underbrace{\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}}_{\textbf{Term 2}}+\underbrace{\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)}_{\textbf{Term 3}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Term 1</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Term 2</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Term 3</mtext></munder><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left(\underbrace{\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}}_{\textbf{Term 1}}-\underbrace{\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}}_{\textbf{Term 2}}+\underbrace{\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)}_{\textbf{Term 3}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Term 1:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex111.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐲</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex112.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#A3.E69" title="Equation 69 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>), we get,</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{y}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{y}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{y}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{y}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex116.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">“zero-masking probability” in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS3" title="3.2.3 SUBS Parameterization ‣ 3.2 Masked Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.3</span></a> <math id="A3.Ex116.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\implies\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{y}}\rangle=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\implies\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{y}}\rangle=1</annotation></semantics></math>; hence,</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Term 2:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex117.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{x}}}+\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\not\in\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\}}\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{x}}}+\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\not\in\{{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}\}}\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex119.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A3.Ex119.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">∵</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.Ex119.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> for <math id="A3.Ex119.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\not\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\not\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.1 Interpolating Discrete Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)) we get:</span></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex121.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.1 Interpolating Discrete Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log{\mathbf{s}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}})_{{\mathbf{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex123.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Using (<a href="#A3.E69" title="Equation 69 ‣ C.3 Concrete Score for MDLM ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>), we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}+\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}+\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Term 3:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex125.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}K\left(\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\left[\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\mathbf{m}}}\left[\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}+\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\not\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}}\left[\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}+\sum_{{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\not\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}}\left[\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex128.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A3.Ex128.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">∵</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because q_{t}({\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}|{\mathbf{x}})=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.Ex128.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> for <math id="A3.Ex128.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\not\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}\not\in\{{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{m}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get,</span></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}\log\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}-\frac{q_{t}({\mathbf{x}}|{\mathbf{x}})}{q_{t}({\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex130.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Substituting the values using (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.1 Interpolating Discrete Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Substituing (<a href="#A3.Ex111" title="In Term 1: ‣ C.5 Deriving MDLM’s NELBO via CTMC ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">86</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.Ex117" title="In Term 2: ‣ C.5 Deriving MDLM’s NELBO via CTMC ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">87</span></a>), and (<a href="#A3.Ex125" title="In Term 3: ‣ C.5 Deriving MDLM’s NELBO via CTMC ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">88</span></a>) in (<a href="#A3.Ex105" title="In Proof. ‣ C.5 Deriving MDLM’s NELBO via CTMC ‣ Appendix C Concrete Score Matching ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">85</span></a>) we get,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex131.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\Bigg[-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\Bigg(\cancel{\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><menclose notation="updiagonalstrike"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\Bigg[-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\Bigg(\cancel{\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 128.0374pt+\cancel{\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}}\Bigg)\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><menclose notation="updiagonalstrike"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></menclose><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 128.0374pt+\cancel{\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}}\Bigg)\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left(-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[-\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left(-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle\left[\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{m}},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex135.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Under the SUBS parameterization, <math id="A3.Ex135.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A3.Ex135.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}={\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>; hence <math id="A3.Ex135.m1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.250em" minsize="1.250em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{m}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> can be dropped:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E89.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boxed{\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boxed{\mathbb{E}_{t\in[0,1],{\mathbf{y}}\sim q_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}})}\left[\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This concludes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experimental details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Likelihood Evaluation</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a single monte-carlo estimate for <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> to evaluate the likelihood. The low discrepancy sampler (<a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Low discrepancy sampler ‣ Appendix D Experimental details ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>) plays a key role in reducing the variance of the estimate as seen in Table <a href="#S5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 5.3 Ablation Analysis ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Avg. Number of Tokens seen</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">training_steps</span>, <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">batch_size</span>, <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">context_length</span>, the number of tokens seen by the AR model is given as:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\texttt{training\_steps}\times\texttt{batch\_size}\times\texttt{context\_length}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">training_steps</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">batch_size</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">context_length</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\texttt{training\_steps}\times\texttt{batch\_size}\times\texttt{context\_length}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">However, this expression doesn’t hold for a diffusion model, since at each training step, a fraction of the input tokens are masked before being fed to the model. Let <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be the probability of a token being masked at a timestep <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. For the log-linear schedule in our experiments, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{m}=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{m}=t</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the expected number of tokens seen by the diffusion model is:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex136.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}[\texttt{training\_steps}\times\texttt{batch\_size}\times\texttt{context\_length}\times p_{m}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">training_steps</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">batch_size</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">context_length</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}[\texttt{training\_steps}\times\texttt{batch\_size}\times\texttt{context\_length}\times p_{m}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{training\_steps}\times\texttt{batch\_size}\times\texttt{context\_length}\times\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}[p_{m}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">training_steps</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">batch_size</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">context_length</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{training\_steps}\times\texttt{batch\_size}\times\texttt{context\_length}\times\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}[p_{m}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{training\_steps}\times\texttt{batch\_size}\times\texttt{context\_length}\times\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}[t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">training_steps</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">batch_size</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">context_length</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{training\_steps}\times\texttt{batch\_size}\times\texttt{context\_length}\times\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}[t]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A4.Ex138.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A4.Ex138.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because p_{m}=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">∵</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because p_{m}=t</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{training\_steps}\times\texttt{batch\_size}\times\texttt{context\_length}\times 0.5." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">training_steps</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">batch_size</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">context_length</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{training\_steps}\times\texttt{batch\_size}\times\texttt{context\_length}\times 0.5.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A4.E91.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A4.E91.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}[t]=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">∵</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">[</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}[t]=0.5</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">LM1B.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>, we train MDLM for 1M training steps with a <span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">batch_size</span> = 512, and a context length of 128. Like <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite> we use a log-linear schedule and hence the number of tokens seen by our model is <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 33" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>33</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 33</annotation></semantics></math>B (<a href="#A4.Ex136" title="In D.2 Avg. Number of Tokens seen ‣ Appendix D Experimental details ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">91</span></a>). Similarly, MDLM trained for 10M steps, saw 327B tokens in expectation. The corresponding AR baseline was trained for 0.5M and 5M steps to ensure a similar number of tokens was seen.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">OWT.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train SEDD and MDLM for 1M training steps with a <span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">batch_size</span> = 512, <span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">context_length</span> = 1024, and log-linear schedule. Hence, these models saw 262B tokens during training. Similarly, the AR model saw the same number of tokens when trained for 0.5M steps with the same <span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">batch_size</span> and <span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">context_length</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Low discrepancy sampler</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To reduce variance during training we use a low-discrepancy sampler, similar to that proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma et al. [29]</a></cite>.
Specifically, when processing a minibatch of <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> samples, instead of independently sampling <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> from a uniform distribution, we partition the unit interval and sample the time step for each sequence <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\ldots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\ldots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math> from a different portion of the interval <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\sim U[\frac{i-1}{N},\frac{i}{N}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\sim U[\frac{i-1}{N},\frac{i}{N}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
This ensures that our sampled timesteps are more evenly spaced across the interval <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, reducing the variance of the ELBO.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Language Modeling</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For our forward noise process, we use a log-linear noise schedule similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. [33]</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We detokenize the One Billion Words dataset following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. [33]</a></cite>, whose code can be found <a href="https://github.com/louaaron/Score-Entropy-Discrete-Diffusion/blob/main/data.py" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">here</a><span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            https://github.com/louaaron/Score-Entropy-Discrete-Diffusion/blob/main/data.py</span></span></span>.
We tokenize the One Billion Words dataset with the <span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bert-base-uncased</span> tokenizer, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al. [26]</a></cite>. We pad and truncate sequences to a length of 128.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We tokenize OpenWebText with the <span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GPT2</span> tokenizer. We do not pad or truncate sequences – we concatenate and wrap them to a length of 1,024. When wrapping, we add the <span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">eos</span> token in-between concatenated. We additionally set the first and last token of every batch to be <span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">eos</span>.
Since OpenWebText does not have a validation split, we leave the last 100k docs as validation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We parameterize our autoregressive baselines, SEDD, and MDLM with the transformer architecture from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. [33]</a></cite>. We use 12 layers, a hidden dimension of 768, 12 attention heads, and a timestep embedding of 128 when applicable. Word embeddings are not tied between the input and output.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We use the AdamW optimizer with a batch size of 512, constant learning rate warmup from 0 to a learning rate of 3e-4 for 2,500 steps. We use a constant learning rate for 1M, 5M, or 10M steps on One Billion Words, and 1M steps for OpenWebText. We use a dropout rate of 0.1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Zeroshot Likelihood</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate zeroshot likelihoods by taking the models trained on OpenWebText and evaluating likelihoods on the validation splits of 7 datasets: Penn Tree Bank (PTB; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Marcus et al. [36]</a></cite>), Wikitext <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, One Billion Word Language Model Benchmark (LM1B; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chelba et al. [8]</a></cite>), Lambada <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>, AG News <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>]</cite>, and Scientific Papers (Pubmed and Arxiv subsets; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cohan et al. [10]</a></cite>).
We detokenize the datasets following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. [33]</a></cite>.
For the AG News and Scientific Papers (Pubmed and Arxiv), we apply both the Wikitext and One Billion Words detokenizers.
Since the zeroshot datasets have different conventions for sequence segmentation, we wrap sequences to 1024 and do not add <span id="A4.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">eos</span> tokens in between sequences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Representation Learning</h3>

<div id="A4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Devlin et al. [15]</a></cite>, we evaluate on all GLUE tasks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite>, but exclude WNLI.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We pre-train a MosaicBERT model on C4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite> for 70k steps, corresponding to 36B tokens. We pad and truncate the data to 128 tokens using the <span id="A4.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bert-base-uncased</span> tokenizer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">MosaicBERT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite> has a similar architecture to <span id="A4.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bert-base-uncased</span> and has 137M parameters, 12 layers, 12 attention heads, a hidden dimension of 768, an intermediate size of 3072, and ALiBi attention bias <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For pre-training, we use the following hyperparameters: A global batch size of 4096 with gradient accumulation, a learning rate of 5e-4, linear decay to 0.02x of the learning rate with a warmup of 0.06x of the full training duration, and the decoupled AdamW optimizer with 1e-5 weight decay and betas 0.9 and 0.98.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For diffusion fine-tuning we use AdamW with a warmup of 2,500 steps from a learning rate of 0 to 5e-5, betas 0.95 and 0.999, and batch size 512. We train for 5k steps total, corresponding to 32M tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For GLUE evaluation, we use the HuggingFace script found <a href="https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/tree/main/examples/pytorch/text-classification" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">here</a><span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/tree/main/examples/pytorch/text-classification</span></span></span>. We use the default parameters for all datasets, except for a batch size of 16, which we found helped with smaller datasets. This includes the default of 3 epochs for all datasets and learning rate of 2e-5.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.7 </span>Diffusion DNA Models</h3>

<section id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset</h5>

<div id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We pre-train the Caduceus MLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite> on the HG38 human reference genome <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schiff et al. [50]</a></cite>, we use character- / base pair-level tokenization. The dataset is based on the splits used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Avsec et al. [3]</a></cite>: the training split comprises of 35 billion tokens covering the human genome. This consists of 34,021 segments extended to a maximum length of 1,048,576 (220 segments). We maintain a constant <math id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{20}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>20</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{20}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens per batch. For the Genomics Benchmark tasks, we use 5-fold cross-validation where we split the training set into 90/10 train/validation splits.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Architecture</h5>

<div id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Caduceus MLM uses as a backbone a bi-directional variant of the data-dependent SSM Mamba block proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al. [22]</a></cite>. This architecture is ideal as it contains inductive biases that preserve reverse complement (RC) equviariance, respecting the inherent symmetry of double-stranded DNA molecules <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, <a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training details</h5>

<div id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All models are pre-trained on 10B tokens (10K steps) and fine-tuned on a generative objective for an additional 50B tokens (50K steps). We use a global batch size of 1024 for a context length of 1024 tokens. Downstream task fine-tuning is performed for 16K steps ( 1B tokens).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For performing Caduceus MLM pre-training, we follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schiff et al. [50]</a></cite> for the model size configuration, and hyperparameter selection. For pre-training, we use a fixed 15% mask rate as done in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Devlin et al. [15]</a></cite>. Of the ’masked’ tokens, 80% are replaced with [<span id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">mask</span>] , 10% are replaced with a random token from the vocabulary, and 10% are left unchanged.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For fine-tuning all Mamba-based models (including Caduceus) on diffusion objectives, we lower the learning rate from 8e-3 to 1e-3. For fine-tuning HyenaDNA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, we lower the learning rate from 6e-4 to 5e-5. Similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al. [22]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schiff et al. [50]</a></cite>, we found that Mamba-based models were robust to higher learning rates. We exclude timestep embeddings for all Diffusion DNA experiments, as we show it has minimal impact on generative performance (see Table <a href="#A5.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ E.5 Time-conditioning ablation on OWT ‣ Appendix E Additional Experiments ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, Suppl. <a href="#A5.SS5" title="E.5 Time-conditioning ablation on OWT ‣ Appendix E Additional Experiments ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We perform downstream task fine-tuning on the final hidden state embedding from pre-training. We perform mean pooling across the sequence length,
which may vary from 200 to approximately 2,000 bps. We report the mean and <math id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> on max/min classification accuracy over 5-fold cross-validation (CV) using
different random seeds, with early stopping on validation accuracy. For each task, we do a hyperparameter sweep over batch size and learning rate and report the values of the 5-fold CV for the best configuration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Genomic Benchmark Task Distributions</h5>

<div id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a subset of the Genomic Benchmark tasks with an emphasis on tasks from Human data. The positive samples for each dataset were generated by selecting samples that were annotated, either computationally or experimentally, in previous work (e.g enhancers, promoters, open chromatin regions (OCR)) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>. These annotations each correspond to subsets of the genome of varying sizes that may exhibit different distributions of DNA than those observed globally over the reference genome.
Due to this, the observed dataset may have a different distribution than the data used for pre-training and calculating perplexity. This might in turn lead to a case where perplexity and downstream performance may not necessarily correlate.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Additional Experiments</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Noise schedule parameterization</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As described in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Continuous-Time Likelihood Bounds ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, the ELBO is invariant to the functional form of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. To demonstrate this, we evaluate MDLM, initially trained using a log-linear schedule on OWT, by replacing the noise schedule with various other noise schedules as mentioned below. Following prior works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>, we parameterize <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=e^{-\sigma(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=e^{-\sigma(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(t):[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(t):[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Various functional forms of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are listed below:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Log Linear <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>.</span> The log linear schedule is given as:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma(t)=-\log\;(1-t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma(t)=-\log\;(1-t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cosine Squared schedule <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>.</span>
The Cosine Squared schedule is given as:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma(t)=-\log\;\text{cos}^{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2}(1-t)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><msup><mtext>cos</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma(t)=-\log\;\text{cos}^{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2}(1-t)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cosine schedule.</span>
The Cosine schedule is given as:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma(t)=-\log\;\text{cos}\left(\frac{\pi}{2}(1-t)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><mtext>cos</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma(t)=-\log\;\text{cos}\left(\frac{\pi}{2}(1-t)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Linear.</span>
The Linear schedule is given as:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma(t)=\sigma_{\text{max}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma(t)=\sigma_{\text{max}}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a very large number. In our experiments we set it to <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{8}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.1 </span>ELBO Invariance</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The function <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible due to the monotonicity assumption in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Interpolating Discrete Diffusion ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, and so we can perform the following change of variables in (<a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 3.4 Continuous-Time Likelihood Bounds ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>):
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\gamma}}\equiv\log(1-\alpha_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜸</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\gamma}}\equiv\log(1-\alpha_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> be a function such that <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\gamma}}=f(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜸</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\gamma}}=f(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> goes through a monotonic transformation to obtain <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math>; hence, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math> is also monotonic in <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonic in <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that the function <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible. Let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we can we have the following diffusion loss:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{NELBO}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>NELBO</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{NELBO}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex139.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{t=0}^{t=1}\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle{\text{d}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{t=0}^{t=1}\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle{\text{d}}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{t=0}^{t=1}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\frac{{\text{d}}}{{\text{d}}t}[\log(1-\alpha_{t})]{\text{d}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtext>d</mtext><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{t=0}^{t=1}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\frac{{\text{d}}}{{\text{d}}t}[\log(1-\alpha_{t})]{\text{d}}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{t=0}^{t=1}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\frac{{\text{d}}}{{\text{d}}t}[f(t)]{\text{d}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtext>d</mtext><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{t=0}^{t=1}\log\langle\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle\frac{{\text{d}}}{{\text{d}}t}[f(t)]{\text{d}}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A5.Ex141.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Substituting <math id="A5.Ex141.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)=\log(1-\alpha_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)=\log(1-\alpha_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{{\bm{\gamma}}=-\infty}^{{\bm{\gamma}}=0}\log\langle{\mathbf{x}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}})},f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}})),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle{\text{d}}{\bm{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝜸</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝜸</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mi>𝜸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{{\bm{\gamma}}=-\infty}^{{\bm{\gamma}}=0}\log\langle{\mathbf{x}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}})},f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}})),{\mathbf{x}}\rangle{\text{d}}{\bm{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A5.Ex142.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:80%;">Change of variables <math id="A5.Ex142.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\gamma}}\equiv f(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜸</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\gamma}}\equiv f(t)</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{{\bm{\gamma}}=-\infty}^{{\bm{\gamma}}=0}\log\langle{{\mathbf{x}}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{\bm{\gamma}},f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}})),\;{\mathbf{x}}\rangle{\text{d}}{\bm{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝜸</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝜸</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝜸</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mi>𝜸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{{\bm{\gamma}}=-\infty}^{{\bm{\gamma}}=0}\log\langle{{\mathbf{x}}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{\bm{\gamma}},f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}})),\;{\mathbf{x}}\rangle{\text{d}}{\bm{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A5.Ex143.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A5.Ex143.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{\bm{\gamma}}\equiv{\mathbf{z}}_{f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝜸</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">≡</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐳</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">f</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝜸</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{\bm{\gamma}}\equiv{\mathbf{z}}_{f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E96.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{{\bm{\gamma}}=-\infty}^{{\bm{\gamma}}=0}\log\langle\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{\bm{\gamma}},{\bm{\gamma}}),\;{\mathbf{x}}\rangle{\text{d}}{\bm{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝜸</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝜸</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝜸</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mi>𝜸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\int_{{\bm{\gamma}}=-\infty}^{{\bm{\gamma}}=0}\log\langle\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{\bm{\gamma}},{\bm{\gamma}}),\;{\mathbf{x}}\rangle{\text{d}}{\bm{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A5.E96.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A5.E96.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{\bm{\gamma}},{\bm{\gamma}})\equiv{{\mathbf{x}}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{\bm{\gamma}},f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝜸</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝜸</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">≡</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝜸</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">f</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝜸</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{\bm{\gamma}},{\bm{\gamma}})\equiv{{\mathbf{x}}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{\bm{\gamma}},f^{-1}({\bm{\gamma}}))</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This new formulation demonstrates that the diffusion loss is invariant to the functional form of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In Table <a href="#A5.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ E.1.1 ELBO Invariance ‣ E.1 Noise schedule parameterization ‣ Appendix E Additional Experiments ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we demonstrate empirically that noise schedules with different functional forms evaluate to the same Likelihood which is consistent with our theory.
However, different schedules lead to different per data point variance. Notably, the log-linear schedule exhibits the lowest variance among all the noise schedules considered.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 9</span>: </span><span id="A5.T9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Likelihood in bits per dimension (BPD) for different noise schedules on OWT dataset, is reported along with the mean and variance associated with each noise schedule per data point. We empirically observe that noise schedules with different functional forms yield the same likelihood, consistent with our theory in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Continuous-Time Likelihood Bounds ‣ 3 Simple Masked Diffusion Models ‣ Simple and Effective Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>; however, different schedules result in different variances.</span></figcaption>
